---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro"
import { SITE } from "../site"
---

<Page
  title="Privacy"
  description="SnarkBrain uses no cookies, ads, analytics or trackers. What little data is involved in visiting or contacting us, and how it's handled."
  lede="No cookies, ads, analytics or trackers."
>
  <p>
    <em>Last updated September 26, 2026.</em>
  </p>

  <h2>Visiting the site</h2>
  <p>
    SnarkBrain doesn't set cookies, run analytics or load advertising or tracking scripts. Fonts, images and video are
    served from this domain, so reading a page doesn't contact any third party.
  </p>
  <p>
    The site is hosted on <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare</a>. Like any web host, it
    processes technical information such as your IP address and browser to deliver pages and protect the site from
    abuse. We don't receive or store that information.
  </p>

  <h2>On your device</h2>
  <p>
    If you switch between light and dark mode, your choice is saved in your browser's local storage so it's remembered
    next time. It never leaves your device.
  </p>
  <p>Search runs entirely in your browser. What you type isn't sent to us or anyone else.</p>

  <h2>Contacting us</h2>
  <p>
    If you email us, we receive your email address and whatever you send. We use it only to read and reply to your
    message, and we don't share it or add you to any list. Ask us to delete your messages at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>
    Fact-checks link to sources such as YouTube, Reddit and court records. Those sites have their own privacy policies,
    which apply once you follow a link. The share buttons on fact-checks are plain links too: nothing is sent to a
    social network unless you click one.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
  </p>
</Page>
